    <ul class="checks">
      <li><span><b>School portals are not a footnote</b>Consulting firms publish university-specific events, resume drops and deadlines that never reach the national careers page. For a lot of students this is the only realistic door.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Prepare before the posting opens</b>Resume, behavioural stories and case basics should be ready in advance. MBB windows can be a few weeks wide, which is not enough time to start from zero.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Use third-party deadline pages as alarms only</b>Management Consulted and Simplify are useful discovery layers. The firm's own page determines the real deadline, every time.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Assume next year is earlier again</b>MBB deadlines have moved one to two months earlier in each of the last several cycles. If you are planning for 2028, do not anchor on this year's dates.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

